# 7. DECLARATION AND EVIDENCE REVIEW

The legacy system made it easy to locate individual declared results.

The new system must do better.

## Requirement presentation

Each requirement should show:

- Short understandable requirement name.
- Applicable rule.
- Student declaration summary.
- Evidence count.
- Human review status, if applicable.

Do not require three nested accordion expansions to reach a document.

## Declaration presentation

Each Student declaration should be easy to scan.

Display:

- Declaration title.
- Relevant values.
- Date or period when applicable.
- Associated evidence.
- Existing human review result when supported.

Keep supporting secondary metadata visually subdued.

## Evidence

Support direct evidence preview.

The reviewer should be able to:

1. Open a declaration.
2. See its evidence.
3. Open PDF or image.
4. Close the viewer.
5. Continue the same review without losing context.

Preserve evidence version history and scoped supplementation semantics.

Do not introduce automatic evidence approval.

Do not reduce multiple declarations into one combined unsupported record.

Preserve ONE_OF / ALL_OF requirements correctly.

