# 8. PROGRESS — CLEAR AND TRUSTWORTHY

The current UI shows too many simultaneous status indicators.

Simplify.

At application level, show a small useful summary such as:

- 2/5 tiêu chí đã xét.
- 1 tiêu chí đạt.
- 1 tiêu chí không đạt.
- 3 tiêu chí chưa hoàn tất.

Use the real canonical human review data.

The exact presentation should follow the actual state model.

Do not count AI preliminary assessments as completed human reviews.

Do not count declarations merely because they exist as reviewed.

Do not conflate:

- Declared evidence.
- Human-reviewed content.
- Criterion outcome.
- Completed Officer assessment.
- Official Committee recognition.

A criterion may require multiple requirement/declaration-level assessments.

Only report it as completed according to the actual existing domain aggregation rules.

## Criterion status

Show ONE main human review state by default.

Examples derived from actual canonical states:

- Chưa xét.
- Đang xét.
- Chờ bổ sung.
- Đạt.
- Không đạt.

If an AI observation exists, do not create a second competing official-looking status badge.

Keep AI advisory information behind the optional AI entry point or a very subtle separate indicator.

