# 12. ROLE-SPECIFIC REVIEW ACTIONS

Reuse the same dossier presentation, but compose only legitimate role actions.

## School Officer

- Read Student declarations/evidence.
- Record School preliminary judgments.
- Add notes.
- Request supplementation.
- Record School recommendation.
- Continue School review.

No per-application City forwarding.

The one-time School batch forwarding workflow remains separate.

## City Reviewer

- Open shared City review queue.
- Inspect Student dossier.
- Record authorized independent human judgments.
- Add notes.
- Request supplementation.
- Complete normal City review.

No mandatory individual Officer assignment.

No ResolutionCase.

No ambiguous-case escalation.

## City Committee

- Inspect original Student dossier.
- View actual School preliminary result.
- View actual City assessment.
- View common School decision attachment.
- Inspect evidence where needed.
- Record authorized official Committee decision.

Do not force Committee members to repeat all City Officer evidence judgments unless the actual approved business contract requires it.

Committee decision controls must remain separate from ordinary criterion-assessment controls.

No fictional meeting, voting, questioning or hearing workflow.

## Authorization

Use actual backend RBAC and resource-scoped ABAC.

Technical ADMIN authority alone does not grant Committee decision permissions.

Never use frontend role labels as the only authorization boundary.

