# 13. AI — ONE OPTIONAL ASSISTANT

AI should not dominate the reviewer workspace.

Use one concise entry point:

**"AI hỗ trợ"**

AI may provide:

- Preliminary criterion assessment.
- Material evidence discrepancies.
- Source-linked findings.
- Concise application review summary.
- Suggested verification actions.

AI must not:

- Record human judgments.
- Automatically approve declarations.
- Automatically submit supplementation.
- Automatically finalize review.
- Make Committee official decisions.

Do not display separate AI status labels on every criterion by default if they reduce clarity.

Do not automatically open AI panels.

Do not make AI analysis a mandatory review step.

No new AI backend subsystem in this phase.

