# 14. RESPONSIVE REDESIGN — MANDATORY

Current review layouts have major responsiveness problems.

Fix the actual parent layout, not only child components.

Inspect:

- Global sidebar.
- Criterion navigation width.
- Main dossier grid.
- Sticky review panel.
- Evidence table columns.
- Overlay stacking.
- Minimum widths.
- Scroll container boundaries.
- AI launcher.
- Demo persona selector.

## Important

Use actual AVAILABLE CONTENT WIDTH as the main responsive constraint.

A 1440px browser with a 250px sidebar and a 300px criterion panel does not have 1440px available for dossier content.

Use container queries where suitable.

Maintain compatible responsive fallbacks.

### Wide desktop

Beautiful professional workspace.

One criterion navigation.

Comfortable dossier width.

Review actions positioned logically.

### Standard laptop

Reduce secondary navigation width.

Allow criterion navigation to become compact.

Do not crush evidence cells.

### Tablet

Prioritize dossier content.

Criterion navigation becomes a compact accessible selector when necessary.

Review actions remain visible.

### Mobile

Single primary content column.

Quick criterion selector.

Easy-to-open evidence.

Touch-friendly judgment controls.

Bottom actions only if they do not obstruct content.

No clipped dialogs or off-screen Save buttons.

### Required viewport checks

320, 360, 390, 430, 768, 1024, 1280, 1440, 1660 and 1920px.

No horizontal page overflow.

No hidden review controls.

No scrolling traps.

No sticky toolbar covering evidence.

No conflicting active criterion.

No Demo selector blocking actions.

No AI overlay blocking official decisions.

